course: dictionary
lesson: 12424
title: Turning things off
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To deactivate something means to turn it off or stop it from working. The prefix de- often means "undo" or "take away", and activate means "make it work", so deactivate is the opposite of activate.
explain: «Mum asked me to deactivate the alarm before we went inside.» The alarm was working, and deactivating it stopped it. Check your meaning by swapping in "turn off": "Mum asked me to turn off the alarm before we went inside" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Deactivate can also mean to close or pause an account so nobody can use it. «Sam decided to deactivate his old game account.» Sam did not smash his computer. He stopped the account from being used, which is what the word means here.
explain: Context helps again. «The hero had only seconds to deactivate the bomb before it went off.» The clues are bomb, only seconds and before it went off, so deactivate must mean stopping the bomb from working in time.
fact: Deactivate is a verb: deactivate, deactivates, deactivated, deactivating.
fact: To deactivate something is to turn it off or stop it from working.
fact: To deactivate an account is to close it or pause it so it cannot be used.
fact: The opposite of deactivate is activate, which means to turn something on or make it work.
fact: In science, heat can deactivate some substances, such as germs and enzymes.
exercise: «Mum asked me to deactivate the alarm before we went in.» What does deactivate mean? | Buy a brand-new one | *Turn it off | Turn it up as loud as possible | Paint it a different colour
exercise: Sam wants to deactivate his old account. What does this mean? | Make it bigger and better | *Close it or pause it so it cannot be used | Turn on a new one | Send messages to all his friends
exercise: Find the opposite of deactivate. | sleep | forget | walk | *activate
test: «The engineer had to deactivate the machine before she could fix it.» Why did she deactivate it? | To make it run faster | *So it would stop working and she could fix it safely | To wake it up | To give it a new name
test: Which form of deactivate is in the past tense? | deactivating | deactivates | *deactivated | deactivation
exam: Which sentence means the same as "Turn off the alarm"? | Please deliver the alarm | Please decorate the alarm | *Please deactivate the alarm | Please activate the alarm
